<title>UK: Druid shares set debut premium.</title>
<headline>Druid shares set debut premium.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in management consultancy Druid Plc set a premium on their first day of trading on the London Stock Exchange on Tuesday.</p>
<p>By 1140 GMT the shares traded at 287-1/2p, 12-1/2p ahead of the placing price of 275p. Volume was 1.8 million shares.</p>
<p>&quot;We are delighted with the response we have received from the market and we greatly look forward to our future as a listed company,&quot; said managing director David Thompson.</p>
<p>The issue, sponsored by SBC Warburg, valued Druid at 62.9 million stg and raised 1.85 million stg net of expenses.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
